.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-CREATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-create - Create a team by paying for its seats


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team create <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a team by paying for its seats. The command prints a Checkout link, opens it in a
browser when it can, and then waits until payment completes and the team exists. The owner uses
one of the seats.

.PP
Paying needs your agreement to the no-refund terms: without --accept-terms the command prints
them and stops. Add --accept-terms to agree and continue.

.PP
Use --no-wait to print the link and return. Ctrl+C or --wait-timeout stops only the waiting; the
team is still created once you pay, and pb team get shows it. Running the same command again
reuses the same order instead of billing twice.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--accept-terms\fP[=false]
	agree to the no-refund terms the command prints; required to pay

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--interval\fP="month"
	billing interval: month or year

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--no-wait\fP[=false]
	print the Checkout link and return without waiting for payment

.PP
\fB--seats\fP=1
	seats to buy, including the owner's (1-128)

.PP
\fB--wait-timeout\fP=15m0s
	how long to wait for payment before returning


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team create acme --seats 5 --accept-terms
  pb team create acme --seats 5 --interval year --no-wait --accept-terms
  pb team create acme --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
